#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101591} :activity/id #uuid "0674df03-7c13-5be8-b206-8215c54adc2f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050898 :topic/id #uuid "6f6a1e18-10c1-5fb2-9f41-d2b49cf97ce7" :topic/math-academy-id 1161} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101591 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186102029 :tutorial/content "Let's think about how to calculate an integral like $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {\\ln x} {x} \\,\\textrm d x.$\n\nNotice that this integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac {\\ln x} {x} \\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\underbrace{\\ln x}_{u} \\cdot\\overbrace{\\dfrac {1} {x}}^{u'} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe've seen integrals like this before, where the integrand consists of a function $u(x)$ multiplied by its derivative $u'(x).$ Such integrals can be solved by substitution.\n\nSo, we let $u = \\ln x,$ which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad   \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\dfrac 1 x \\,\\textrm{d}x={\\textrm{d}u}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       \\int \\dfrac{\\ln x}{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \t&=\\int \\ln x\\cdot \\dfrac {1} {x} \\,\\textrm d x \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = \\int u \\, \\textrm{d} u \\[5pt]\n                                                                &=  \\dfrac{1}{2}u^2  +C \\[5pt]   \n                                                                &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln^2 x +C}\n$$\n\nAfter solving an integral using substitution, we should always double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({ln}^{2}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "f20c3f56-ce97-548d-a8e0-c4a604acbc18" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8918 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "859100d6-9232-5a35-9f92-1ff67d69671a" :step/math-academy-id 118773 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101592}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100608 :question/id #uuid "8ea17e06-1248-510c-9e71-c57da0cb0d02" :question/math-academy-id "e-14405"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050628} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050690}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101144} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101145} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101318} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269163} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269169} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269173} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269175} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290275} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290276} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290508} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297382} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374531} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401887} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441898} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441899}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"} :step/id #uuid "3b90fdb1-78e3-5033-ad6e-5d7b6eda947e" :step/math-academy-id 118774 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101593}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100817 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100609 :question/id #uuid "1579f932-6e7f-5daa-b001-54a9f6c236ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14406"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101371} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101374} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101536} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250156} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250157} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290277} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290281} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297379} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297381} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297384} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297385} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297386} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374607} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384656}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"} :step/id #uuid "bfc6f2ca-3c8f-5042-8e12-9a9d8d3e183b" :step/math-academy-id 118778 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101594}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101594 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186102030 :tutorial/content "Let's evaluate the following definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^4} \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }\n$$\n\nWe'll use the change of variable method, which comprises three steps:\n\n**Step 1:**  Change the variable.\n\nLet's introduce the new variable $u = \\ln x.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{x}\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\textrm{d}u = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2:**  Find the new limits of integration.\n\nWe use the table below to change our limits of integration from $x$ to $u{:}$\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\n**Step 3:** Evaluate the integral in the new variable $u.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{u}^{1/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =6(2-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "2add6e6b-5049-58e9-8095-b87e840d0844" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8931 :tutorial/title "Definite Integrals"} :step/id #uuid "fbecfd22-fc2c-53b8-959b-315e1af4f8fa" :step/math-academy-id 118782 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101595}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101595 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100610 :question/id #uuid "d2f49acf-ed91-510d-a0f1-41c50eeef9e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-14422"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101451} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101452} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101535} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269179} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269180} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269181} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269182} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297454} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297472} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297478} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297482} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297532} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319100} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319101} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320812} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320813} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320814} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332728} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332750} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342050} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342051} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342052} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342053} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374617} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374624} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375067} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375070} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375342} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441900} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490225} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490242} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490258} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490321}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"} :step/id #uuid "8be2d12d-5050-599a-aca3-294a974cd35b" :step/math-academy-id 118783}] :activity/title "Integrating Logarithmic Functions Using Substitution" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101029}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490333} :activity/id #uuid "336ad382-de21-59dd-a8b8-5d390abe01d7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050898 :topic/id #uuid "6f6a1e18-10c1-5fb2-9f41-d2b49cf97ce7" :topic/math-academy-id 1161} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490333 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59077802-2ece-52ce-8fdb-8f6f3735b72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489730} {:answer/id #uuid "da84991b-fcac-5426-a689-60bfacfa87a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489996} {:answer/id #uuid "df6c29bc-d773-5ece-9a45-14b4359b35cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489999} {:answer/id #uuid "eed896f0-f769-50fb-a53d-7bc14aff6cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490029} {:answer/id #uuid "f14b3a35-0151-5e3a-b9bf-83c572725766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490032}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490032} :answer-field/id #uuid "a108c977-d111-5123-bfa0-9f9dd2b6376b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "633f13a2-1c12-5a0e-ade7-b4d04e14c842" :question/math-academy-id "q-13844" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3}{2x{ln}^{2}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x).$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡8$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3}{2x{ln}^{2}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {(-{u}^{-1})|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{u})|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "07385d24-63ec-535c-82de-17f626a1096d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490352}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490352 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "588a64f8-b007-597a-90a1-13bc0deadb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489726} {:answer/id #uuid "58d74548-f1c5-5c19-af0c-64a5b689a324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489727} {:answer/id #uuid "64f36bf8-3759-5b50-8859-73b64d5b2c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{log}_{2}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489752} {:answer/id #uuid "ae420e08-ae64-53a3-b2a8-a61252329c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489897} {:answer/id #uuid "fba1a44c-3ac0-56fc-b34d-91572dd0f45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490061}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489727} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e61d7a6-a656-53b9-8d80-257f6bbc76cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "43a38f2f-26ab-5a55-9c36-de9ec5e565a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-31615" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{4}^{8}\\frac{1}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{8}\\frac{1}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{8}\\frac{1}{{log}_{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4b42cd91-b82a-535b-b5c5-adcf55aee423" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490378}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490361 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6a9f60-c08f-5467-a283-a5c875e998cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489583} {:answer/id #uuid "311cb6a0-4004-536b-aff8-04d49cb5cc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489625} {:answer/id #uuid "abe6da9b-8429-54a3-ba90-b2deefe451bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489892} {:answer/id #uuid "f50f90e5-5553-5d0c-bfdb-c4fbba7c5236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490044} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4aa3c7-4608-5feb-8e43-09317d7d8264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490044} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8df4958-daa0-55e3-96a1-d8edb4b2bd89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ee507cc2-c5c1-5dca-b8f8-28391520da63" :question/math-academy-id "q-49552" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/4$ | ${e}^{3}/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{e/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7b445d8f-dac4-57e3-8a85-d397d960305e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490369}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490369 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f292278-673c-5eba-880c-7cda055f8171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330511} {:answer/id #uuid "5dac8132-bf52-5344-825a-5d6616a1cdd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330784} {:answer/id #uuid "83aeb76a-c46c-5da9-b6b1-d3b2c07f5e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331119} {:answer/id #uuid "884a0de8-2fb3-540c-834e-7021c6f3a3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331163} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4580e3-6e2d-5fe8-9d8c-28fc47a327cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331902}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330784} :answer-field/id #uuid "d90e8da3-8c2b-5ff0-aa8c-d768bd2f0c85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "06ae8c49-a573-55e1-8d24-c78494f9b5b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49606" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9c8216e1-395f-5076-8f10-f59a07984539"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490378 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16b7494e-bb79-5b12-9236-a587f999330d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489565} {:answer/id #uuid "1b976c74-2288-5edb-ac14-b1435c6814f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489578} {:answer/id #uuid "4a39aa0a-e274-5fb2-8704-b394c3cd5dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489687} {:answer/id #uuid "65a94067-f449-5e05-8e2b-89087734bd4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489754} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3b6154-88e4-5ca3-9c7b-ddeffecf3bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489798}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489798} :answer-field/id #uuid "3273c5e4-90f1-5aee-9f26-60f52ccd89f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "29e8aaaf-e383-5b29-a6be-9cfefb451c7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-31616" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bb02c843-1dc2-58cd-9106-2495f4a3db6b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490361}}] :activity/title "Integrating Logarithmic Functions Using Substitution" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489502}]}
